## Conclusions
In summary, we present novel 3D-dual-linked hexaiminobenzene MOFs with tailored properties as bifunctional oxygen electrocatalysts demonstrating excellent intrinsic electrical conductivity, crystallinity, and chemical compatibility. The MOFs with precisely controlled $\mathbf{M}^{2+}$ species in quintet-shelled hollow spheres possess a large surface area $(2298~\mathrm{~m}^{2}~\mathrm{~g}^{-1})$ with active redox sites, fast electron and mass transfer pathways, and effective ${\bf M}(\mathrm{{\scriptscriptstyleII}}){-}{\bf N}_{4}$ moieties, outperforming the oxygen bifunctional reversibility $(\Delta E=0.627\mathrm{V})$ of the benchmark noble metals. DFT computations revealed that the electronic structures of the MOFs, with intrinsic conductivity and $\mathbf{O}_{2}$ adsorption capability, facilitate their superior bifunctional performance. Notably, rechargeable liquid ZABs with Mn/Fe-HIB-MOF demonstrated a record-breaking cycle life of over $1000{\mathrm{h@10~mA~cm}}^{-2}$ with trivial voltage fading and energy density (1027 W h $\operatorname{kg_{Zn}}^{-1}$ over the time-scale of rechargeable ZABs. Furthermore, a robust, flexible FBN membrane with superionic conductivity $(64~\mathrm{mS~cm^{-1}}$ ), excellent water retention, and low anisotropic swelling has been invented. Flexible ZABs with $\bf{M n/F e}$ -HIB-MOF and the FBN membrane displayed unprecedented cycling stability for $600\mathrm{~h~}$ (3600 cycles $\textcircled{2}25$ mA $\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ ) and excellent mechanical robustness. This record-breaking
